 "Taller de haiku": "Haiku workshop",
 "5 · 7 · 5 sílabas para atrapar un instante": "5 · 7 · 5 syllables to capture a moment",
 "Biblioteca municipal · jueves de poesía": "Public library · poetry Thursdays",
 "Animación por párrafos: cada idea entra con su clic (Subir). Leerla en voz alta antes de pasar a la siguiente.": "Animation by paragraph: each idea comes in with its click (Up). Read it aloud before moving on to the next.",
 "¿Qué es un haiku?": "What is a haiku?",
 "<div style=\"font-weight:700;color:#c8102e\">Tres versos</div><div>De cinco, siete y cinco sílabas. Nada más: ni título ni rima.</div>": "<div style=\"font-weight:700;color:#c8102e\">Three lines</div><div>Of five, seven and five syllables. Nothing else: no title, no rhyme.</div>",
 "<div style=\"font-weight:700;color:#c8102e\">Un instante</div><div>Lo que se ve, se oye o se huele ahora mismo. Sin explicar lo que se siente.</div>": "<div style=\"font-weight:700;color:#c8102e\">A moment</div><div>What you see, hear or smell right now. Without explaining what you feel.</div>",
 "<div style=\"font-weight:700;color:#c8102e\">Una estación</div><div>Una palabra que la sugiera: lluvia, almendro, chicharra, hojas…</div>": "<div style=\"font-weight:700;color:#c8102e\">A season</div><div>A word that hints at it: rain, almond tree, cicada, leaves…</div>",
 "Tres clics, un verso cada uno: sus palabras aparecen solas, una tras otra, al ritmo de la lectura (150 ms entre palabras), y al final del verso el sello rojo cuenta las sílabas.": "Three clicks, one line each: its words appear by themselves, one after another, at reading pace (150 ms between words), and at the end of the line the red stamp counts the syllables.",
 "Un haiku, palabra a palabra": "A haiku, word by word",
 "Lluvia": "Gentle rain",
 "el": "the",
 "charco": "puddle",
 "guarda": "holds",
 "cielo": "heaven",
 "que": "that",
 "Haiku escrito para este taller.": "Haiku written for this workshop.",
 "Primer clic: las sílabas saltan una a una con su número. Segundo: se dibuja el arco bajo la sinalefa y aparece la explicación; al final, el total con campanilla.": "First click: the syllables jump one by one with their number. Second: the arc is drawn under the elision and the explanation appears; at the end, the total with a chime.",
 "Contar sílabas": "Counting syllables",
 "el charco guarda el cielo": "the puddle holds the heaven",
 "char": "pud",
 "co": "dle",
 "guar": "holds",
 "da‿el": "the",
 "cie": "hea",
 "lo": "ven",
 "<b>Sinalefa:</b> «guarda el» se lee «guar-dael». La vocal final y la inicial se unen en una sola sílaba.": "<b>Elision:</b> in Spanish, two vowels can merge into one syllable (“guarda el” is read “guar-dael”). In English, count the syllables as you say them.",
 "Clic 1: se tachan «agua» y «del» a la vez. Clic 2: se tacha «refleja» y se escribe encima, a mano, «guarda». Clic 3: fuera «azul». La diapositiva siguiente usa Transformar: las palabras que quedan viajan a su sitio.": "Click 1: “water” and “of” are struck out at the same time. Click 2: “reflects” is struck out and “holds” is handwritten over it. Click 3: out goes “blue”. The next slide uses Morph: the remaining words travel to their place.",
 "Corregir un borrador": "Editing a draft",
 "agua": "water",
 "del": "of",
 "refleja": "reflects",
 "azul": "blue",
 "12 sílabas: sobra el agua, sobra el azul (el cielo ya lo es) y «refleja» explica demasiado.": "Too many syllables: the water is redundant, so is the blue (the sky already is), and “reflects” explains too much.",
 "Transformar: «el», «charco», «el» y «cielo» son los mismos objetos que en el borrador y se deslizan a su sitio; «guarda» pasa de la letra a mano a la de máquina. Al llegar, el recuento confirma las siete sílabas.": "Morph: “the”, “puddle”, “the” and “heaven” are the same objects as in the draft and slide into place; “holds” changes from handwriting to typewriter font. On arrival, the count confirms the seven syllables.",
 "El verso, limpio": "The clean line",
 "el · char · co · guar · da‿el · cie · lo  =  7": "the · pud · dle · holds · the · hea · ven  =  7",
 "Un clic por estación: la hoja sube y sus tres versos aparecen solos, uno detrás de otro, con una pausa (retardo) entre verso y verso para leerlos.": "One click per season: the leaf rises and its three lines appear by themselves, one after another, with a pause (delay) between lines to read them.",
 "Tres estaciones": "Three seasons",
 "PRIMAVERA": "SPRING",
